/-! ## Moonshine connection -/

/-- For a divisor `dim | MonsterOrder`, the "moonshine box" is the corresponding
    subgroup in `ZMod MonsterOrder`. This associates each irrep dimension with a
    sublattice of the Monster modular group. -/
noncomputable def moonshineBox (dim : ℕ) : AddSubgroup (ZMod MonsterOrder) :=
  subgroupBox MonsterOrder dim

/-! ## The "golden ratio" of a moonshine group

For a pair of primes `(p, q)` and a sequence of coefficients `c(n)`, the
"moonshine golden ratio" is the asymptotic slope `ln q / ln p` of the
log_p / log_q trajectory. For the Monster with (p,q) = (2,3), this is `ln 3 / ln 2`. -/

/-- The moonshine golden ratio for a pair of primes (p, q) is ln(q)/ln(p).
    For the Monster with (2, 3), this equals ln(3)/ln(2) ≈ 1.585. -/
noncomputable def moonshineGoldenRatio (p q : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  Real.log q / Real.log p

/-- The Monster's golden ratio with the canonical prime pair (2, 3). -/
noncomputable def monsterGoldenRatio : ℝ := moonshineGoldenRatio 2 3

/-
The moonshine golden ratio for (2,3) equals log(3)/log(2).
-/
theorem monsterGoldenRatio_eq :
    monsterGoldenRatio = Real.log 3 / Real.log 2 := by
  rfl

